course: dictionary
lesson: 5626
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives three meanings for limb, so use the words around it to choose the right one. «A squid has eight arms plus two longer tentacles, ten limbs in all.» Here the sentence counts limbs as body parts that a creature moves with, so limb means an arm or a leg.
explain: «Signs of a broken bone include not being able to use the limb.» You can break a bone in an arm or a leg, and you use a limb to move, so limb means an arm or a leg here too. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The word tree is a clue. «Do not climb on weak tree limbs» means large branches of a tree. «Out on a limb» is a phrase with its own meaning: it means alone, with an idea that others do not support. You cannot work out a phrase word by word, so learn it as a whole.
fact: A limb is an arm or a leg.
fact: A limb can also be a large branch of a tree.
fact: «Out on a limb» means alone, with an idea others do not support.
fact: Signs of a broken bone include a crack heard, an odd shape, and pain right on the bone.
fact: The context, meaning the words around a word, tells you which meaning is right.
exercise: «Never cut a bite, suck out venom or tie a tight cord around the limb.» In this sentence, what is a limb? | A tree branch | A cord | A bite | *An arm or a leg
exercise: Sam says, «Don't climb on those weak tree limbs.» What does limb mean here? | Pain in the arm | Alone, with an idea others do not support | Dangerous wind | *A large branch of a tree
exercise: Maya says, «She is out on a limb with that idea.» What does out on a limb mean? | Very happy and busy | Climbing high in a tree | Hurt in both legs | *Alone, with an idea others do not support
test: «If you can't use the limb, a doctor should look.» What is a limb in this sentence? | A tree trunk | A bone in the sky | *An arm or a leg | A branch
test: In «A squid has eight arms plus two longer tentacles, ten limbs in all», what are the limbs? | Leaves on a tree | *The parts a creature moves with, like arms and tentacles | Stones on the beach | Hard shells on the sea floor
exam: In «Signs of a broken bone include... not being able to use the limb», which meaning of limb fits? | A large branch of a tree | Alone, with an idea others do not support | A small bird | *An arm or a leg
